# Framer Copy Editing — Three-File Sync

When editing any visible text on a page, you MUST update all three locations:

1. **Page HTML file** (e.g. `index.html`) — the server-rendered markup.
2. **Page component `.mjs` bundle** — the React component that hydrates the page. Search all `.mjs` files for the exact text. Replace every occurrence (text may repeat per responsive breakpoint — use `replace_all`).
3. **`assets/searchIndex.json`** — update the matching entry under the page's URL path (e.g. `"/"`).

If only the HTML is updated, React hydration will overwrite the change with the stale value from the JS bundle.

## Finding the right `.mjs` file

- Search all `.mjs` files for the exact string being changed.
- Or: in the HTML, find `data-framer-hydrate-v2` on `<div id="main">` to get the `routeId`, then search `.mjs` files for content associated with that route.
